                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "*Message to the developer*\nI saw your post and decided to give your project a try and I wanted to share my thoughts with you.  I appreciate what you're trying to do as a single developer and applaud you for it, I imagine it isn't easy, but it wouldn't be fair to you and your goals in game development if I wasn't honest and sincere about your work... \nI see what you were trying to do with the game but there isn't much here.  I understand it's your first project, but here were a couple things I came across.\n\n- The voice acting all sounded like it was the same voice actor and just sounded like someone was just reading a piece of paper for all of it, as if they weren't trying to make it sound believable.\n- There's not much to do in your game in terms of content; I stood on a planet and I threw a ball.. that's it\n- Unless reading the game description I would not have understood what the story was.\n\nHere's what I applaud you for doing \n+ You're doing something in game development, keep it up!! Keep your dreams going!\n+ Your story was something I wish had more depth!! Good choice.\n+ Thank you for allowing the community to try your project.\n+ Being on the planet was pretty, would have been awesome if I could move around on it.\n\nI don't want to come across too harsh, but I love the fact that there are people like you trying to make products for people like us.  Thank you so much for your support in the Vive community and I look forward to seeing what else you do.",
